# G053 — Library Catalog

*v2. See `library-catalog.md` for prose: title/copy/patron triples, holds
queue with FIFO semantics, auto-fulfillment on return, overdue detection.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Book Club Coordinator

[book-club-coordinator @club-members @book-title
    IN ORDER TO
        place a hold for every member on a shared title
        notify each of their position in the queue
        and let returns auto-fulfill forward

    @title <- [catalog[search-by-name {query: @book-title}]]:first

    concurrent [
        for @member in @club-members
            @hold <- [catalog[place-hold
                                {title-id: @title:id, patron-id: @member:id}]]
            @pos  <- [catalog[hold-queue {title-id: @title:id}]]
                     :index-of @hold:id
            <- @sarah{notify @member about position: @pos}
    ]
    join

    where
        every hold has status "waiting"
        and the queue is sorted by placed-at
        and positions are unique
        || -> #queue-inconsistent @resistance:reason
]

---

## Verb Surface

[catalog
    new
    add-title            {title}
    add-copy             {copy}
    check-out            {copy-id, patron-id, duration-days}   ;; || already-checked-out
    return-copy          {loan-id}                              ;; also fulfills next hold
    renew                {loan-id, additional-days}             ;; || has-waiting-hold
    place-hold           {title-id, patron-id}
    cancel-hold          {hold-id}
    hold-queue           {title-id}
    available-copies     {title-id}
    search-by-subject    {prefix}                               ;; tree-prefix search
    search-by-author     {name}
    search-by-name       {query}
    overdue              {now}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: return triggers fulfillment automatically

[catalog[return-copy {loan-id: @loan}
    where
        the copy is marked available
        and if a hold queue exists, the oldest hold is promoted
            to a new loan pointing at this copy
        and the promoted hold's patron is notified via the sync side channel
]

The v1 described this as "wait-and-wake"; in Innate the wait is the
holder's hold record and the wake is a natural side-effect of return.

---

## Overdue detection as scheduled choreography

at @every 1 day
    @overdue-list <- [catalog[overdue {now: @today}]]
    for @loan in @overdue-list
        <- @patrons{@loan:patron-id, remind about overdue: @loan}

---

## Demo

[demo
    @cat <- [catalog[new]]
    [catalog[add-title {title: {id: 1, name: "1984", author: "Orwell",
                                  subjects: ["fiction/dystopian"]}}]]
    [catalog[add-copy {copy: {id: 101, title-id: 1}}]]
    [catalog[add-copy {copy: {id: 102, title-id: 1}}]]

    @loan1 <- [catalog[check-out {copy-id: 101, patron-id: 1, duration-days: 14}]]
    @hold1 <- [catalog[place-hold {title-id: 1, patron-id: 2}]]
    @hold2 <- [catalog[place-hold {title-id: 1, patron-id: 3}]]

    -> [catalog[hold-queue {title-id: 1}]]:length    ;; -> 2
    -> [catalog[available-copies {title-id: 1}]]:length  ;; -> 1 (copy 102)

    ;; copy 101 returns; hold1 is auto-fulfilled
    [catalog[return-copy {loan-id: @loan1:id}]]
    -> [catalog[hold-queue {title-id: 1}]]:length    ;; -> 1 (only hold2 left)
]
